    "body": "## What and why\n\nThe corrected donor learner's adjacent Prefix pass offers no target-winning alternative at five residual positions. Add an opt-in `prefix_transaction: \"gradient_vector_prefix\"` that derives four quantized vectors from the complete original Prefix gradient, evaluates all four at one original epoch, and atomically commits the lowest-loss protected candidate before the existing Generate pass. This tests coordinated finite movement without adding parameters, serving cases or weakening the seventeen-reference/380-guard protection.\n\nThe selected vector is reproduced from compact evidence before commit, preserving the constructor's cache cap. Configuration, recovery, journals and positive artifact authority distinguish the new policy from the unchanged default.\n\n## Result\n\nDecision: **KEEP the implementation; NOT YET PROMOTED as a model.** The integrated source passes **25/25 focused tests** and the optimized production build. The final PR head `c03cd878cce70c144ca95ee37de60d75734d1756` reruns all 25 successfully and passes named formatting, claim wording and diff checks. The dated validation record binds source `df613c194`, both executable hashes and costs; the final head changes only documentation from that executed revision. The native fixture uses two authored rows with a six-token vocabulary and exercises the production selection/commit helpers, actual scorer/reducer, donor/incidence replacement, guard veto and rollback, and a subsequent Generate update. It does not execute the complete 391-row parent construction.\n\nAn initial clamp-test expectation failed (24/25 passed): the policy correctly preserved the original fractional master for an unchanged native code. The test-only correction and failed log are retained. Both mathematical and adversarial source reviews pass the corrected source.\n\nNo actual-parent vector fit or complete-answer evaluation occurred. Accepted **8/512** development replies and the separate, unselected corrected-donor **9/15** remain unchanged. The next model run is admitted only after this PR is merged and its workspace is cleaned.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Checks run at this exact head (commands and outcomes posted on this PR)\n- [x] Research record: `docs/labs/prefix-vector-transaction-2026-10-09/README.md`\n- [x] New entry at the top of `docs/integration/current-state.md`, with **Next:**\n- [x] Every document this change makes stale is updated; dated prior results remain scoped history\n- [x] STATUS.md / ROADMAP.md / #2028 table: measured model position and milestone status unchanged\n- [x] README updated within its existing Training section; crate README documents the opt-in field\n- [x] `python3 scripts/check_claim_wording.py` passes at final head\n- [x] After merge: verify on fresh `origin/main`, delete the branch and worktree, preserve evidence in iCloud, apply hygiene, and report the result on M2\n\nReferences #2030\n",
